                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ba7abb29-9dac-437a-b8f9-fc04548dda90",
                                                "sense_id": "0fd81097-2f1a-37b6-a27d-8b5582a31742",
                                                "text": "Some general ideas on clipping, viewporting, and windowing can be found in Rogers and Adams."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "43bb9090-e799-416b-b2f2-b8cb038ad342",
                                                "sense_id": "0fd81097-2f1a-37b6-a27d-8b5582a31742",
                                                "text": "Viewporting is an operation that takes the portion of the picture that has been mapped into the square region delimited by -1,+1,-1,+1 and further maps it into a rectangular subregion of the screen (a viewport)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "17ea08df-515f-47df-a541-bed6add3297f",
                                                "sense_id": "0fd81097-2f1a-37b6-a27d-8b5582a31742",
                                                "text": "The main thing I want you to take away from this chapter is knowing where to start and creating a very simple viewported web site using nothing more than an extra <meta> tag and simple HTML."
